# The gliquid wheel is a BUILD INPUT, not source. It is produced from the
# gliquid_python checkout (see src/requirements.txt for the exact command) and
# dropped here for `docker build`. Keeping it untracked is deliberate: this repo is
# public, `*.webp` in .gitattributes has its LFS filter commented out, and a binary
# artifact committed here would be in plain git forever.
src/wheels/

# Byte-compiled artifacts (this tree is COPY'd into the image as-is).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test suite and its framework deps, held back from the repo for now. Nothing here is a
# build input: the Dockerfile installs only requirements.txt, so the image is unaffected.
src/tests/
src/requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache/

# The loose per-system assets this commit removed. They are served from
# gliqviz/matrix_shards/ now, and the generator writes new ones to dev/data/matrix_assets/
# in the gliquid workspace, never here. Ignored rather than merely deleted so that a stray
# `git add -A` in a tree that still has the old directory cannot put 810 MB back.
src/app/gliqviz/matrix_assets/
